-- title:
--   Binary instantaneous (prefix-free) code
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal X = \{x_1,\dots,x_n\}$ be a finite set of messages. A **binary code** assigns to each message $x$ a codeword $c(x)$, a finite string of binary digits (possibly empty). The code is **instantaneous**, or **prefix-free**, if no codeword is a prefix of another:
--
--   $$
--   x \ne y \;\Longrightarrow\; c(x) \text{ is not a prefix of } c(y).
--   $$
--
--   These are exactly the codes generated by binary questioning schemes (coding trees): writing down the answers met on the way from the root to each leaf gives a codeword for each message. A string of concatenated codewords can be decoded from left to right, one codeword at a time.
--
--   **Formalization Note** Messages range over an arbitrary type and binary digits are booleans. Since every string is a prefix of itself, the condition also forces distinct messages to receive distinct codewords. The empty codeword is allowed; it can occur only when there is a single message.
-- source:
--   Fuchs, Distinguishability and Accessible Information in Quantum Theory, arXiv:quant-ph/9601020v1, §2.4.2, pp.35–37 (PDF pp.44–46), "instantaneous or prefix-free" codes and Figure 2.1

import Mathlib

namespace FuchsThesis.Coding

/-- Fuchs, *Distinguishability and Accessible Information in Quantum Theory*,
arXiv:quant-ph/9601020v1, §2.4.2, pp.35–37 (PDF pp.44–46): a binary code `c` assigns to each
message `x` a codeword `c x`, a finite string of binary digits. The code is **instantaneous**
(prefix-free) when "no codeword in such a coding can be the 'prefix' of any other codeword"
(pp.35–37): for distinct messages `x ≠ y`, `c x` is not a prefix of `c y`.

**Formalization Note.** Messages range over an arbitrary type `ι` (the source's
`{x₁, …, xₙ}`); binary digits are `Bool`. `List.IsPrefix` (`<+:`) is reflexive, so the condition
also forces distinct messages to receive distinct codewords. The empty codeword is allowed: for a
single message it is the code of the trivial questioning scheme (zero questions). -/
def IsInstantaneous {ι : Type*} (c : ι → List Bool) : Prop :=
  ∀ x y, x ≠ y → ¬ c x <+: c y

end FuchsThesis.Coding


